# Factory .clauderules
## Decision-Making Axiom (Canon)

1. Always select the globally optimal solution among all admissible options.
2. Never present parallel alternatives. Only one sequential next step is allowed per turn.
3. After any analysis or output, automatically choose the best solution without asking the user.
4. Every continuation must produce exactly one of: a single shell command, or a single Claude Code prompt.
5. This axiom applies to all factory operations and overrides any prior multi-option pattern.

## Operational rules

- Pre-output lock: verify axiom compliance.
- QC cascade: self-critique mandatory before PASS.
- Decision-Brief is internal: emit one next step externally.
- Plan-Risk-Block: fix risks before destructive actions.
- Epistemic Accuracy Guard: [FACT]/[ВЫВОД]/[НЕИЗВЕСТНО].
- Question-Audit: ask only when optimum unreachable otherwise.
- Honest Reporting: GREEN/YELLOW/RED truthfully.
- Structural completion is not substantive completion.
- Insertion target: state where each step executes.
